  "body": "### User need\n\nA user wants to machine a heater block from copper and state the actual workpiece material on its stock. The material picker has six presets. Copper is missing. On build `e6e04f5d0`, MCP `set_stock_material` also refused copper as an unknown material. Selecting brass would use the brass cutting data for this part.\n\n### Requested change\n\nAdd a copper workpiece material to the document and stock pickers. Accept the same material through MCP. Give it a stable project-file value so the choice survives save and reopen. State which copper grade or range the preset covers. The reporter did not specify an alloy.\n\nThe material selection can supply cutting data for operations. Document the source and scope of any copper-specific cutting data. If a tool has no applicable copper data, keep that limitation visible.\n\n**Done means:** A user can select copper for stock, save the project and reopen it with copper still selected. A test sets copper through MCP and reads it back. A cutting-data test covers the intended behavior for copper. Existing project material values continue to load.\n\nSuggested triage: enhancement, P6, effort:high, area:3d, source:agent. This is an unscheduled request. Material selection can change the feeds used in posted programs.\n\n[Workpiece material table](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/e6e04f5d0/crates/tools/src/cutting.rs#L60-L132)\n",
